{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.hoefsmit_vtx_pow_not_isHermitian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.hoefsmit_vtx_pow_not_isHermitian","kind":"theorem","line":424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L424-L466","doc":"**Consequence for the literal reading**: for `1 < q ≤ 23/20` (`q₀`\nincluded) and the actual Hoefsmit data, no vertex power `V^k` with `1 ≤ k ≤ 5`\nis symmetric — so none is `Matrix.PosSemidef`, and the literal `SDPSelected`\nadmits no γγ word of `2 ≤ 2k ≤ 10` crossings. The corresponding claim for all\n`k` is exactly `vtx_pow_isHermitian_iff_scalar`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.h_sq_le_of_q_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.h_sq_le_of_q_le","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L410-L422","doc":"`h² ≤ 1/10` for every `1 ≤ q ≤ 23/20` (the proton pin `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` is\ninside; there `h² ≈ 0.0437`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.chi_signs_of_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.chi_signs_of_small","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L394-L408","doc":"The sign pattern `(−, −, +, −, −)` of `χ_(2,1)(V^k)`, `k = 1..5`, for every\n`0 < h² ≤ 1/10` — the step-3 table as a theorem on an interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_ne_zero_of_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_ne_zero_of_small","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L366-L392","doc":"`α_k ≠ 0` for `k = 1..5` whenever `0 < h² ≤ 1/10` (`x = h²`): no vertex\npower up to the fifth is symmetric on that whole interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L340-L364","doc":"**`V³ = 1 ⇔ h = 0`**: the cube of the vertex is the identity exactly at the\nundeformed point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_isHermitian_iff_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_isHermitian_iff_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L312-L338","doc":"**`V^k` is symmetric iff it is `±1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_isHermitian_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_isHermitian_iff","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L291-L310","doc":"**`V^k` is symmetric iff `α_k = 0`** (with `t = −1 − h²`), for `0 < q` and\n`b ≠ 0`: the off-diagonal defect of `V` is `b(q + q⁻¹) ≠ 0`, and that of `V^k`\nis `α_k` times it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.isHermitian_iff_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.isHermitian_iff_off","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L278-L289","doc":"A real `2×2` matrix is Hermitian (= symmetric) iff its two off-diagonal\nentries agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_five","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L264-L270","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_four","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L257-L262","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_three","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L251-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_two","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L245-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_vtx_pow_one","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L237-L243","doc":"Closed-form traces of the first five vertex powers (`x = h²`): the probe's\n`χ_(2,1)` column is this Chebyshev recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L223-L235","doc":"`V³ − 1 = h²·((2 + h²)·V + 1)`: the defect from the identity is exactly `h²`\ntimes a matrix whose `(0,1)` entry is `(2 + h²)·q·b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_three","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L211-L221","doc":"**The vertex cube is the `q`-deformed identity**:\n`V³ = (2h² + h⁴)·V + (1 + h²)·1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_eq_lin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_pow_eq_lin","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L202-L209","doc":"`V^k = α_k V + β_k 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_sq","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L194-L200","doc":"Cayley–Hamilton for the vertex: `V² = (−1 − h²)·V − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_det","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L184-L192","doc":"`det V = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_trace","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L175-L182","doc":"`tr V = −1 − h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.hoefsmit_a_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.hoefsmit_a_mul","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L165-L173","doc":"The Hoefsmit relations `a(1 − q⁴) = h`, `h = q − q⁻¹` force\n`a·q·(1 + q²) = −1` whenever `q² ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.stdImage_vertexPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.stdImage_vertexPow","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L155-L163","doc":"The vertex power's image is the power of the vertex image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_entries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx_entries","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L151-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.vtx","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L147-L149","doc":"The `(2,1)`-block image of the γγ vertex `σ₀σ₁⁻¹` under the Hoefsmit data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.pow_off_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.pow_off_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L132-L137","doc":"The off-diagonal defect of `M^k` is `α_k` times that of `M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_pow_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.trace_pow_eq","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L125-L130","doc":"The trace of `M^k` in terms of the `lin` coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.pow_eq_lin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.pow_eq_lin","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L114-L123","doc":"`M^k` is the `lin`-combination of `M` and `1` whenever `M² = t·M − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.sq_eq_of_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.sq_eq_of_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton for a `2×2` matrix of determinant one**, entrywise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_five","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_four","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_three","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_two","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L82-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_succ","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin_zero","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder.lin","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaVertexOrder.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The linearisation coefficients: `M^k = (lin t k).1 • M + (lin t k).2 • 1`\nfor any `M` with `M * M = t • M - 1` (`pow_eq_lin`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}